All figures completed successfully!

======= KEY FINDINGS SUMMARY =======

1. Most common barrier across all ages: Time (~40-44% of patients)

2. Middle-aged (45-59) with Transportation barriers:
   - Non-compliance rate: 41.9% (vs 22.4% overall for middle-aged)
   - Fisher exact: OR=3.38, p=0.0017 (statistically significant)

3. Young adults (18-44) with Multiple barriers:
   - Non-compliance rate: 31.6% (highest in young group)

4. Older adults (60+) with Time barriers:
   - Non-compliance rate: 29.8% (highest in older group)

5. Minimal improvement rates by age group:
   - Young adults: 52.0% (highest minimal improvement)
   - Middle-aged: 46.3%
   - Older adults: 46.9%

6. Significant improvement rates:
   - Middle-aged Transportation: 32.6% (best)
   - Young adults Time: 19.7% (worst)

7. Satisfaction (mean, 1-10):
   - Middle-aged: 5.79 (highest)
   - Older adults: 5.23 (lowest)
   - Older adults Transportation: 4.92 (lowest across all groups)
